\section{2. Method}

We conducted three online, within-subjects experiments in English-speaking young adults who consume alcohol, the target group of our message sample (see below). Study 1a measured alcohol craving and mechanism-related responses to a broad range of professional and peer-produced pro- and anti-alcohol messages reflecting the current media environment. Study 1b introduced non-alcoholic comparison conditions. Study 2 conceptually replicated Studies 1a/b using a subset of alcoholic messages and a different task design. All participants provided informed consent and study procedures were approved by our university's ethical review board (protocol number anonymized).

\subsection{2.1 Reproducibility package}
The studies reported here were not pre-registered. Measures, data, and analysis code are available on our OSF page (\href{https://osf.io/cg3fn/files}{https://osf.io/cg3fn/files}). This reproducibility package includes descriptions and sources of all stimuli. Original stimuli are available upon request. Only Study 2 participants completed additional measures concerning orthogonal research questions about meat consumption (see reproducibility package). 

